{title: The Vow at Mizpah}
{subtitle: Judges 11:1–3; 11:4–11; 11:12–28; 11:30–31; 11:32–33; 11:34–40}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Em] | [Em] | [D] | [C] |
| [D] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]Jephthah the Gileadite was a [D]mighty warrior
[C]But the son of a prostitute in [G]that [Am]land
His brothers drove him out of [Em]the father's house
Say[C]ing you are the [D]son of another [Em]woman
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He fled to the land of Tob among [D]outcasts
Where [C]worthless men gathered around [G]him
When [Am]Ammon made war up[Em]on Israel
The [C]elders [D]of Gilead [Em]sought him out
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They [C]said come be our commander [G]in battle
[Am]And Jephthah asked why now in [Em]trouble
If [C]the Lord gives the [D]enemy [Em]into my hand
[C]Then I shall [D]be your head [Em]in Gilead
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
He sent messengers to the king of [D]Ammon
[C]Arguing for the land of Is[G]rael
[Am]But the king paid no heed to the [Em]message
So [C]Jephthah made a [D]vow to the [Em]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
If you [Am]give the Ammonites into my [Em]hand
Who[Am]ever comes out shall belong to [Em]God
He [Am]struck down twenty towns in [Em]the valley
A [C]crushing blow that [D]subdued the en[Em]emy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
When he came home to Mizpah [D]in triumph
His [C]daughter met him with tambourines and [G]dance
[Am]She was his only child in [Em]this world
And [C]he tore [D]his clothes in [Em]deep sorrow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Oh my [Am]daughter you have brought me to my [Em]knees
I [Am]have opened my mouth to the [Em]Lord
She said [Am]do to me as you have [Em]vowed
[C]Grant me two [D]months to weep on the [Em]hills
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
And [C]so it be[D]came a custom in Is[Em]rael
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
